<title>BELGIUM: Commission fixes olive oil production aid.</title>
<headline>Commission fixes olive oil production aid.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission on Monday adopted a regulation setting the estimated production of olive oil for the 1995/96 marketing year, it said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The estimated production is put at 1,417,200 million tonnes and the unit amount of the production aid that may be paid in advance is set at 116,32 ecus per 100 kg the regulation states.</p>
<p>Small producers whose average production does not amount to 500 kilograms are not affected by the regulation.</p>
<p>The document lists the production and advances as:</p>
<p>		    Production		  Advances</p>
<p>Greece	    0.270 million t	   322 million ecus</p>
<p>Spain	     0.310 million t	   370 million ecus</p>
<p>France	    0.000 million t	   0.2 million ecus</p>
<p>Italy	     0.554 million t	   696 million ecus</p>
<p>Portugal	  0.040 million t	    47 million ecus</p>
<p>Total advances (all producers)	    1435 million ecus.</p>
<p>The regulation has been approved by the EU oils and fats management committee and will enter into force on the day it is published in the EU Official Journal.</p>
</text>
